OL,3,GNEWSAStolen Sycamore Gap sapling
OL,4,Amystery continues
OL,5,
OL,6,FPolice have been unable to identify the
OL,7,Fculprit behind the theft of a sapling
OL,8,Fgrown from the felled Sycamore Gap
OL,9,Ftree.
OL,11,FThe young tree, which was believed to
OL,12,Fhave been stolen in June, was planted
OL,13,Fat Wray Castle, near Ambleside,
OL,14,FCumbria, in April 2026.
OL,16,FIt was one of 49 grown from seeds taken
OL,17,Ffrom the sycamore, which was illegally
OL,18,Ffelled in September 2023.
OL,23,APub: 01-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
